            <ArticleTitle>Creatine kinase-myocardial band isoenzyme elevation after percutaneous coronary interventions using sirolimus-eluting stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1397-401, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We evaluated predictors of increased periprocedural creatine kinase-MB isoenzyme levels after implantation of sirolimus-eluting stents with an intent to fully cover the diseased segment. The total stent length per patient (predisposing factor) and elective use of glycoprotein IIb/IIIa (protective factor) were independent predictors of increased creatine kinase-MB isoenzyme levels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
